Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: propagate initial buffer queue failures

The conversion path starts the video device before queueing its internal
capture buffers. A deferred driver start can fail from the first QBUF, and
subsequent QBUF calls can fail with EIO after the queue enters an error state.
Ignoring those errors makes Camera::start() report success without enough
capture buffers, leaving applications waiting for requests that cannot finish.

Check each initial queueBuffer() result. On failure, stop the pipeline through
the existing cleanup path and return the original error without submitting
more buffers. Earlier successful submissions remain owned by that stop path.

This corrects error propagation. It does not repair the Surface rear-camera
restart failure that exposed it, change successful submission order, or add
retries. Function-level tests exercise the actual start() body with controlled
dependency failures; hardware and full package validation remain separate.

---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1388,8 +1388,13 @@ int SimplePipelineHandler::start(Camera *camera, [[maybe_unused]] const ControlList *controls)
 		}
 
 		/* Queue all internal buffers for capture. */
-		for (std::unique_ptr<FrameBuffer> &buffer : data->conversionBuffers_)
-			video->queueBuffer(buffer.get());
+		for (std::unique_ptr<FrameBuffer> &buffer : data->conversionBuffers_) {
+			ret = video->queueBuffer(buffer.get());
+			if (ret < 0) {
+				stop(camera);
+				return ret;
+			}
+		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
